{% if include_examples %}
Examples:

Example 1

Task:
The input contains an integer n (1 <= n <= 100) followed by a string of length n consisting of lowercase Latin letters.

Extract:
precondition: n satisfies 1 <= n <= 100.
precondition: The input string has length n.
precondition: Every character of the input string is a lowercase Latin letter.

Do not produce:
precondition: The input string has length n and consists of lowercase letters.

Reason:
It combines multiple obligations.

Example 2

Task:
Return any longest string.

Extract:
postcondition: The returned string is one of the candidate strings.
postcondition: The returned string has maximal length.
postcondition: If multiple strings have maximal length, any one may be returned.

Do not produce:
postcondition: Return the longest valid string.

Reason:
It combines multiple guarantees.

Example 3

Task:
A substring consists of consecutive characters. Occurrences may overlap.

Extract:
invariant: A substring consists of consecutive characters.
invariant: Occurrences may overlap.

Do not produce:
postcondition: Count overlapping occurrences.

Reason:
This is a semantic rule, not a supplier guarantee.

Example 4

Task:
Time limit: 2 seconds. Memory limit: 512 MB.

Extract:
resource_bound: Execution time must not exceed 2 seconds.
resource_bound: Memory usage must not exceed 512 MB.
